{
  "title": "Ulnocarpal Abutment Syndrome",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/hand/6048/ulnocarpal-abutment-syndrome",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Jul 18 2024",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "Summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Ulnocarpal Abutment Syndrome is a common source of ulnar sided wrist pain secondary to excessive impact stress between the ulna and the carpal bones (primarily lunate).",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made with PA wrist radiographs showing positive ulnar variance and sclerosis of the lunate.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment includes a trial of rest and splinting for minimally symptomatic patients. Operative ulnar shortening procedures are indicated depending on severity of symptoms.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathoanatomy",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "in a wrist with **+2 mm ulnar variance** approximately",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**40% of the load goes to the ulna**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "60% to the radius",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "in a normal **neutral wrist** approximately",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**20% of the load goes to the ulna**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**80% to the radius**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Associated conditions",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "positive ulnar variance can be seen in the setting of:",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "scapholunate dissociation",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "TFCC tears",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "lunotriquetral ligament tears",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "radial shortening from previous Colles fracture",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "pain on dorsal side of DRUJ",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "increased pain with ulnar deviation of wrist",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "pain with axial loading",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "ulna sided wrist pain",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**Ballottement test**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "dorsal and palmar displacement of ulna with wrist in ulnar deviation",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "positive test produces pain",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**Nakamura's ulnar stress test**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "ulnar deviation of pronated wrist while axially loading, flexing and extending the wrist",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "positive test produces pain",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "**fovea test**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "used to evaluate for TFCC tear or ulnotriquetral ligament tear",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "performed by palpation of the ulnar wrist between the styloid and FCU tendon",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "recommended views",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**AP radiograph with wrist in neutral supination/pronation and zero rotation**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**required to evaluate ulnar variance**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "**pronated grip view**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**increases radiographic impaction**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "**arthrography** can show TFCC tear and lunotriquetral ligament tear",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**ulna positive variance**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**sclerosis of lunate** and ulnar head",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "MRI",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "evaluate for TFCC tears which may be caused by ulnocarpal impingement and often influences treatment",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Differential",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Ulnar styloid impaction syndrome",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "DRUJ instability or arthritis",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "TFCC tear",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "LT ligament tear",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "pisotriquetral arthritis",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "ECU tendonitis or instability",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Lunotriquetral coalition",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "supportive measures",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "may attempt supportive measures as first line of treatment",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**ulnar shortening osteotomy**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "most cases of ulnar positive variance",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "most cases of DRUJ incongruity",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "Wafer procedure",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/6048/images/wafer.jpg",
                  "caption": "AP wrist radiograph of the Wafer procedure"
                }
              ],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "ulnar positive variance <4mm",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "faster return to work time and lower complication rate compared with ulnar shortening osteotomy",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "-1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "technique",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "2 to 4mm of cartilage and bone removed from under TFCC arthroscopically",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "Darrach procedure (ulnar head resection)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/6048/images/darrach.jpg",
                  "caption": "Darrach procedure"
                }
              ],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "reserved for lower demand patients",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "complications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "risk of proximal ulna **stump instability**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "Sauvé-Kapandji procedure",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/6048/images/sauve.jpg",
                  "caption": "AP wrist s/p sauve procedure"
                }
              ],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**good option for manual laborers**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "technique",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "creates a distal radioulnar fusion and a ulnar pseudoarthrosis proximal to the fusion site through which rotation can occur",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "ulnar hemiresection arthroplasty",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/6048/images/hemiresection.jpg",
                  "caption": "Ulnar Hemiresection Arthroplasty"
                }
              ],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**usually requires an intact or reconstructed TFCC**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "appropriate treatment option in the presence of post-traumatic DRUJ with concomitant distal ulnar degenerative changes",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "ulnar head replacement",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/6048/images/ulnar%20head%20replacement_moved.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "severe ulnocarpal arthrosis",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "salvage for failed Darrach",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "outcomes",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "early results are promising, long-term results pending",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Techniques",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Ulnar shortening osteotomy**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**approach**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**subcutaneous to ulna**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "technique",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "often combined with arthroscopic TFCC repair",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
